Z||000000||pontiacs4me||04-24-2001||03:04 AM||||Im wanting to build up a early 90s 3800.  Bigger cam, port the heads and intake, bigger throttle body and injectors, forged pistons, fully balanced bottom end, headers. etc, etc.  But I cant find forged pistons anywhere.  I can only find cast hyperutectic.  I want to put a 60 shot of NOS to it.  Im looking for about 220 horse at the crankshaft, no NOS.  There is a guy here in Wichita that does custom engine coatings, he puts a thermal coat on the top, and an anti friction coating on the skirt, It costs 18 dollars a piston.  Does anybody know about these coatings?  He tells me that the coating will protect the pistons under Nitrous conditions.  He mentioned Venoila pistons, but they will cost me over a hundred bucks each!  Anybody know if someone else makes them, other than custom made?  Do these engines have hydraulic flat tappet or roller cams?  Ive been looking on comp cams website, and they only show flat tappet, up to like 97 3800's, but a friend of mine told me the series 2 engines were roller?  I want to get an early 90's engine for ease of wiring install.  thanks in advance.||||reg||1
